Recent analyses of lepton flavor universality (LFU) violating $b 	o c 	au 
u$ transitions have led to several $U_1$ leptoquark interpretations, which could see a significant impact on the LFU pattern in other $b 	o c 	au  ar{
u}$ transitions. Notably, we examine how these interpretations affect the decay of $\Lambda_b$ to a proton and a tau lepton, also assessing the influence of potential deviations in the $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ transition on the $U_1$ leptoquark model. By exploring contributions from nine $b 	o c 	au  ar{
u}$ operators, we identify how the $U_1$ leptoquark signal in $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ can be affected by deviations in the $\Lambda_b 	o 	au  ar{
u}$ transition. Furthermore, we establish the current experimental limits on branching ratios and CP asymmetry in $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$, which can be used to test the $U_1$ leptoquark model through the $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ transition.
